@* Collapsible's Overview, written by hand after Accordion's: show more, your own trigger, and open
   from the server or C# (code). Accessibility and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<TextBlock>A collapsible is one section that the user opens and closes, without an accordion's frame. It suits a single section most users can skip. It's a native <Code>details</Code> element, so it opens and closes <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">with JavaScript off</Anchor> too.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>For several sections, see <Anchor Href="docs/components/accordion">Accordion</Anchor>. For a panel over the page, see <Anchor Href="docs/components/popover">Popover</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Show more</Heading>
<TextBlock>A "show more" is a line of text with a chevron that opens the section below it. It suits advanced options, or details most users can skip. Set <Code>Label</Code> to the text beside the chevron.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="collapsible-usage" />

<Heading Level="2">A custom trigger</Heading>
<TextBlock>The trigger is what the user clicks to open the section. To replace the label and chevron with inline content of your own, set <Code>Trigger</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="collapsible-custom-trigger" />

<Heading Level="2">Opening from the server or C#</Heading>
<TextBlock>A collapsible can start open, such as when a form post left an error inside it. Set <Code>Open</Code> to start it open. On interactive pages, to read and set whether it's open from C#, set <Code>@@bind-Open</Code>.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@OpenCode</Code>
<TextBlock>The browser keeps track of whether it's open, not the server. On static pages, after a form post or reload, it's open or closed as <Code>Open</Code> sets.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string OpenCode = """
        @* Open after a post that found a problem in the advanced options. *@
        <Collapsible Label="Advanced options" Open="_advancedInvalid">…</Collapsible>

        @* Interactive pages: follow it, or open it from C#. *@
        <Collapsible Label="Details" @bind-Open="_detailsOpen">…</Collapsible>
        """;
}
